# Marketplace plugins resolve from the GL3 registry; everything else keeps
# coming from registry.npmjs.org.
#
# SCOPED, never a bare `registry=` line. A global registry would route every
# dependency — zod, argon2, fastify — through this host, and Verdaccio's npmjs
# uplink hides that until the host is down, at which point every build
# everywhere fails.
#
# No `_authToken`: written for a public-read registry, so installs need no
# credential and nothing secret lives in the repo. If reads ever require auth
# the line is `//npm.gl3.dev/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}` — commit the literal,
# npm expands the env var at read time. The Docker stages must then switch
# from `COPY .npmrc` to `RUN --mount=type=secret`, because a token baked into
# a layer stays readable from the image forever.
@gl3-plugins:registry=https://npm.gl3.dev
